From: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 22:28:52 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: ppe: offload transparent bridge flows

Use the native QSDK L2 flow mode for untagged flows within a common
bridge instead of programming peer MACs into shared routing interfaces.
The flow selects its physical or virtual egress port and checks its
source port, preserving both Ethernet addresses and TTL/Hop Limit.

Authorize wireless injection from an installed bridge flow and its exact
peer MACs. Run injection before the software flowtable so surviving VP
hooks keep their hardware path across flowtable recreation. Keep routed
MAC and hop checks on routed flows. Withdraw
bridge entries when topology, addresses or MTU change; hold RTNL before
the flow lock across bridge validation and publication; retain the normal
resource ownership and quarantine transaction on teardown failures.

Expose the programmed and hardware forwarding modes in the bounded
on-demand flow dump, so bidirectional hits can be checked directly.
Tagged/DSA bridge domains still require their own VLAN editor and domain
encoding; the existing routed and PPPoE paths remain independent.

Link: https://github.com/everything411/qsdk/tree/21a8d13393aa8c7d2abf806e62a8dac2ba7af52f
Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>
